Trustpilot has made me question my online marketing plans and budgets and it should make other SMEs wary of the claims of Trust and Transparency&#128561;

Fake TP Trustboxes, Reviews and Trustscores makes it harder to compete against the sector domination approach of Google Partners who pay TP for reputation management&#128681;

This has not just affected my company in the UK it affects European and US small businesses and self employed who are targeted by corporate scammers&#128122;

Trustpilot helps scams affect others across Europe and the US&#127384;

Examples include how victims reviews for Action Direct UK on Trustpilot were prevented and stopped even after the company was investigated by the claims management regulator and &quot;voluntarily&quot; handed back their licence... reality they were making false claims and defrauding consumers and deceiving the regulator until investigated&#128561;

Other Fields Group websites Debt Survival and Endeavour Law that pays Trustpilot but does not invite reviews⁉️

Or the quickie and managed divorce gaming of Trustpilot&#128681;

Check Rapid Data reviews and gaming and hacked reviewer accounts on a pays for enhanced features account⌨️

It is an example the #fiedsdatarecoveryscam &#128126;

Fields websites helped by Trustpilot include Datenphoenix, Clinique De Donnees, Salvataggio Dati and Clinica De Datos to name just a few that have used fake TP Trustboxes and fake Reviews

It has practically destroyed my Trust in the reviews collection system and raised data protection concerns - how can “verified order” reviews be created in a TP account without the account &quot;owners&quot; knowing ?
Trustpilot refuses to explain this “data breach”

It made me realise I could not use Trustpilot until they answer my concerns but they keep trying to hijack my company reviews despite me asking them to remove my company website

It affects my company revenues / planning and has meant we saw an increase in the numbers of victims of the #fieldsdatarecoveryscam operated by “ethical hacker Dr Jxxx Hxxx Wxxx who is a conservative member of parliament and his father “Professor” Dr Dxxx Hxxx Wxxx is an expert witness to the courts on computer forensics and fox hunting. Involved in many document spooling operations bribery, deception and Lush Dates for Sugar Daddys

It is a GDPR Data Protection / Global Finance / Google Manipulation / antitrust issue that hijacks companies reviews, deceives consumers and will damage good companies when they try to stop paying Trustpilot

Trustpilot targets content and marketing budgets. The data harvested is then sold on and the content generated used to generate google ads revenue

There is little incentive for Trustpilot to remove any content unless the website is paying for reputation management, 20 reviews per page gives several placeholders for ads even if the company does not pay for reviews collection or claim their reviews

The “special fraud / compliance / fake review software detection is a scam itself - I pointed out hundreds of fake reviews every night for months - nothing has changed after 6 years

But consumers and businesses are being Trustjacked for their content and google contacts and in the past facebook contacts

TP is operating as a Danish Troll Mafia Type operation to hijack companies reputation management

Tactics include scraping reviews from other websites marking them “verified order” and displaying them on Trustpilot

Staff at Trustpilot are involved and there was one case where a TP employee had gained access to Trustpilot emails and was holding Trustpilot to ransom. How many more knew about this, what else is stolen, sold or held for ransom or blackmail

Businesses are running scared because Trustpilot has such power with Google it can make or break their online marketing and SEO - thats what happened to me - I realised my company was being targeted with fake reviews, it led to me finding Fields Associates and Trustpilot fake positive reviews and fake trustboxes

Trustpilot owner Pxxx Hxxxx Mxxxx on BBC world business - says trustpilot operates a “Freemium” but it has a cost whether a company pays to play and win or refuses (as Trustpilot sales would have prospects believe)

No mention of a cover up of the flawed flagging system abuse by companies paying Trustpilot

Trustpilot said it was “partnering” with Paypal and Visa and others to use TPs reviews as a merchant validation / credit worthiness
Incentivising fake reviews to get better bank, finance, google advertising rates&#128176;
Trustpilot says it has 600,000 companies collecting reviews on Trustpilot - it is a lie&#128561;
Even TPs own reviews and Trustscore is Gamed
Full of “verified order” reviews for trustpilot not intended for Trustpilot⏰&#129512;

